        "prompt": "Find EF.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$EF=\\dfrac{119}{13}$.",
          "worked": "The right triangles ABE and ACB share the angle at A, so they are similar by AAA. Corresponding sides give $\\frac{AE}{AB}=\\frac{AB}{AC}$, hence $AE=\\frac{5^2}{13}=\\frac{25}{13}$. Similarly, the right triangles CDF and CAB are similar, so $CF=\\frac{CD^2}{CA}=\\frac{25}{13}$. As A,E,F,C occur in this order on the diagonal, $EF=AC-AE-CF=13-\\frac{25}{13}-\\frac{25}{13}=\\frac{119}{13}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      }
